    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d135">

                <pb facs="0382" n="352" sameAs="frus:frus1949v01/pg352"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">
                    S/S–NSC Files:
                    Lot 63D351: NSC 52 Series</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Report to the National Security Council by the Acting
                        Executive Secretary</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lay</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-08">July 8, 1949</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    NSC 52/1</p>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Governmental Programs in National Security and
                        International Affairs for the Fiscal Year</hi> 1951</p>
                <p>The President, in his letter requesting the advice of the National Security
                    Council on the subject, which was circulated as NSC 52,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d135-f1"/>
                    <pb facs="0383" n="353" xml:id="pg353"/> stated that he would establish
                    tentative fiscal limits for planning purposes in developing budget programs for
                    the Fiscal Year 1951, which would be provided to the Council by the Director of
                    the Bureau of the Budget.</p>
                <p>A summary tabulation of these planning limits (Enclosure A), as provided by the
                    Director of the Bureau of the Budget, is circulated herewith for the information
                    of the National Security Council and referred to the special staff committee
                    designated to draft a Council response to the President’s letter.</p>
                <p>Also enclosed, for reference purposes (Enclosure B), are pertinent extracts from
                    the letters by the Director of the Bureau of the Budget to the respective
                    Departments and Agencies responsible for preparing budget estimates for each of
                    these programs.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">James</hi> S. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lay,
                            Jr.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>




                <xi:include href="d135-a1.xml" xpointer="d135-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d135-a2.xml" xpointer="d135-a2"/>
            </div>
